{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Sacrifices.</b> According to the plain sense, this does not speak of Israel, for He already warned against idolatry in the second commandment. Rather, it is said only on account of the ger, and the verse after it is stated on account of him, that he must not lie with an animal and must not sacrifice to idolatry, for such is the custom of a foreign people. Now the condition for dwelling in the land of Israel is that one not lie with an animal, and it says \"to Elohim\" — who was accustomed to be worshipped from aforetime, and the word Elohim includes the angels as well." "<b>To YHWH alone.</b> Only to the honored name alone, which is the name of essence, and no other shall intermingle with Him."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Resolved הגר as 'the ger' (the resident alien) rather than 'the convert,' reading it as the noun in context."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:26.368311335Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}